  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 107 PM MDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nThursday will be our best chance of showers and thunderstorms \nas the monsoon flow will be enhanced by a mid level disturbance \nin the moderate NW Flow aloft. The Flash flood threat this day \nwill be high at any of the burn sites, but the Aspen Acres will \nespecially be under the gun due to the moist unstable upslope \nflow which will affect the mtns/plains interface\n\nFor Friday, scattered to likely showers and storms will continue \nover the mtns and valleys, but the airmass over the plains will \nlikely be more stable and only isold showers and storms are \nexpected. The rain could be heavy and burn scar flash flooding \nthreat will continue. Friday should be the \"coolest\" day across \nthe fcst area. \n\nFor the weekend...flow aloft weakens. Quite a bit of moisture will \nbe trapped under the ridge that is fcst to rebuild over the region \nand we will see scattered storms will continue over the mtns, but \nover the plains it is likely to be dry and it will once again get \nquite hot with temps getting well into the 100s over a good part of \nthe plains. \n\nNext week it will be a bit cooler be a bit cooler with showers and \nstorms over the mtns/valleys and isold storms plains.",
